      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n* **Functionality:**\n  * **Short Read on `GET_STATUS` (`enable_download`, lines 204–213):** `libusb_control_transfer` returns the byte count transferred on success (`\u003e\u003d 0`). Checking only `if (ret \u003c 0)` misses a 0-byte short read (`ret \u003d\u003d 0`), leaving `status` at its initial `0` value and misinterpreting an empty response as status `0`. Check `if (ret \u003c static_cast\u003cint\u003e(sizeof(status)))`.\n  * **Missing Null-Handle Precondition Guard (`find_dfu_interface`, line 273):** Unlike `enable_download()`, `find_dfu_interface()` (and its caller `dfu_detach()`) does not check `if (!dev_handle_) return false;` before calling `libusb_get_device(dev_handle_)`, which dereferences a null pointer if called before `init()` or after `release()`.\n  * **Zero `wTransferSize` Validation (`find_dfu_interface`, lines 314–318):** If a malformed DFU functional descriptor specifies `wTransferSize \u003d\u003d 0`, overwriting `transfer_size_` with `0` causes the chunking loop in `dfu_download()` to stall with 0-byte transfers; fall back to `kDfuDefaultTransferSize` when the parsed transfer size is `0`.\n  * **Resource Leak on Repeated Initialization (`init` / `wait_for_device`, lines 128–176):** Calling `init()` or `wait_for_device()` when `ctx_` or `dev_handle_` is already active overwrites `ctx_` without releasing the existing USB handle or context, and `wait_for_device()` loops forever if `poll_interval_ms \u003c\u003d 0`. Call `release()` before re-initializing.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:**\n  * Extracting the pure DFU functional descriptor TLV parser out of `find_dfu_interface()` into a standalone helper function separates pure byte-buffer parsing from `libusb` device I/O so it can be unit-tested independently.\n* **Code Simplicity:**\n  * **Unreachable Post-Loop Code (`find_dfu_interface`, lines 333–338):** Because the loop body unconditionally returns `true` at line 327 upon finding a DFU interface, reaching line 331 guarantees `dfu_interface_` is `-1`. The `if (dfu_interface_ \u003c 0)` check is redundant and `return true;` at line 338 is unreachable dead code.\n  * **Duplicated Cleanup (`init` / `wait_for_device`, lines 142–143, 171–172):** Reuse `release()` on failure paths instead of manually repeating `libusb_exit(ctx_); ctx_ \u003d nullptr;`.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:**\n  * **In-Class Member Initializers (lines 68–74, 116–119):** Initialize `dev_handle_`, `ctx_`, `dfu_interface_`, and `transfer_size_` at their member declarations and use `RtsUsbDevice() \u003d default;`.\n  * **Typed Durations / No Magic Multipliers (line 167):** Replace `usleep(poll_interval_ms * 1000)` (which uses a raw `1000` conversion factor and `\u003cunistd.h\u003e`) with `std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(poll_interval_ms))` (or a named constant).\n  * **Type Alignment \u0026 C++ Style (lines 106, 239, 289):** Change `detach_timeout_ms` in `dfu_detach()` from `unsigned int` to `uint16_t` to match the 16-bit USB `wValue` parameter of `libusb_control_transfer`, and drop the redundant `struct` keyword on `const libusb_interface_descriptor *alt`.\n* **Security:**\n  * Bounds checks in `find_dfu_interface()` (`off + 1 \u003c alt-\u003eextra_length`, `desc_len \u003d\u003d 0`, `off + desc_len \u003e alt-\u003eextra_length`, `desc_len \u003e\u003d kDfuDescMinLen`) properly prevent out-of-bounds reads on malformed USB extra descriptors.\n* **Testing:**\n  * **Missing Unit Tests for DFU Functional Descriptor Parsing:** While hardware control transfers require a physical or mocked USB device, the DFU functional descriptor TLV parser (lines 298–323) is pure buffer-parsing logic and has no automated unit tests. Please extract it into a helper and add `gtest` coverage for exact minimum length (`kDfuDescMinLen`), off-by-one short descriptors (`kDfuDescMinLen - 1`), truncated descriptors (`off + desc_len \u003e extra_length`), zero-length descriptors (`desc_len \u003d\u003d 0`), multiple TLV entries, and `wTransferSize \u003d\u003d 0`.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:**\n  * This CL has `Size: L (+339, -0)` with 339 lines of production code and 0 lines of tests, exceeding the 250-line limit for non-test changes and combining vendor-specific runtime control with USB DFU descriptor discovery and detachment (including parsing `transfer_size_`, which is only consumed in the follow-up `dfu_download` CL).\n  * **Proposed Split Plan:**\n    1. **CL 1:** Add the base `RtsUsbDevice` USB lifecycle management (`init`, `wait_for_device`, `open_silent`, `release`) and RTS5817 vendor-specific download-mode control (`enable_download`).\n    2. **CL 2:** Add USB DFU interface discovery (`find_dfu_interface`), `dfu_detach()`, and the extracted DFU functional descriptor parser helper with its `gtest` unit tests.\n* **Commit Message:**\n  * State the high-level motivation (\"why\" a self-contained `libusb` tool is needed rather than external `dfu-util`), remove low-level diff narration (`\"The class owns the libusb context and device handle, so copying is disabled\"`), and update `TEST\u003d` to reflect the unit tests. See the inline comment on `/COMMIT_MSG` for copy-pasteable descriptions.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/46b34316-d342-48c7-a7f3-1c5d7cf82dbc)",
