      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Prevent Resource Leaks on Re-Initialization, Deduplicate Cleanup, and Avoid Magic Unit Multipliers:**\n\n1. **Release existing resources before re-initializing:** Both `init()` and `wait_for_device()` call `libusb_init(\u0026ctx_)` directly, which overwrites `ctx_` and leaks `dev_handle_` and the previous `libusb_context` if called when a device or context is already open. Calling `release()` at the start of both methods makes them safe against repeated calls, and calling `release()` on the error paths avoids duplicating `libusb_exit(ctx_); ctx_ \u003d nullptr;`.\n2. **Use `\u003cchrono\u003e` / `\u003cthread\u003e` (or a named constant) instead of `usleep(poll_interval_ms * 1000)`:** The literal `1000` in `usleep(poll_interval_ms * 1000)` is an unnamed unit-conversion constant, and passing `poll_interval_ms \u003c\u003d 0` would cause `while (waited \u003c timeout_ms)` to loop indefinitely. Using `std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(poll_interval_ms))` (from `\u003cchrono\u003e` and `\u003cthread\u003e`) eliminates both the raw `1000` multiplier and the C `\u003cunistd.h\u003e` header:\n\n```cpp\nbool RtsUsbDevice::init(uint16_t vid, uint16_t pid)\n{\n\trelease();\n\n\tint ret \u003d libusb_init(\u0026ctx_);\n\tif (ret \u003c 0) {\n\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"Error: libusb_init() failed: %s\\n\",\n\t\t\tlibusb_error_name(ret));\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n\n\tif (!open_silent(vid, pid)) {\n\t\tfprintf(stderr,\n\t\t\t\"Error: device %04x:%04x not found.\\n\"\n\t\t\t\"Is the device connected and accessible?\\n\",\n\t\t\tvid, pid);\n\t\trelease();\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"Device %04x:%04x opened.\\n\", vid, pid);\n\treturn true;\n}\n\nbool RtsUsbDevice::wait_for_device(uint16_t vid, uint16_t pid,\n\t\t\t\t   int timeout_ms, int poll_interval_ms)\n{\n\tif (timeout_ms \u003c 0 || poll_interval_ms \u003c\u003d 0)\n\t\treturn false;\n\n\trelease();\n\n\tint ret \u003d libusb_init(\u0026ctx_);\n\tif (ret \u003c 0) {\n\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"Error: libusb_init() failed: %s\\n\",\n\t\t\tlibusb_error_name(ret));\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n\n\tfor (int waited \u003d 0; waited \u003c timeout_ms; waited +\u003d poll_interval_ms) {\n\t\tif (open_silent(vid, pid)) {\n\t\t\tprintf(\"Device %04x:%04x opened.\\n\", vid, pid);\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\t\t}\n\t\tstd::this_thread::sleep_for(\n\t\t\tstd::chrono::milliseconds(poll_interval_ms));\n\t}\n\n\trelease();\n\tfprintf(stderr, \"Error: device %04x:%04x did not re-enumerate \"\n\t\t\t\"within %d ms.\\n\", vid, pid, timeout_ms);\n\treturn false;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/46b34316-d342-48c7-a7f3-1c5d7cf82dbc)",
