      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Check for Short Reads on `GET_STATUS` Control Transfer:** `libusb_control_transfer` returns the number of bytes actually transferred on success (`\u003e\u003d 0`). If the device responds with a 0-byte packet (`ret \u003d\u003d 0`), `ret \u003c 0` is false and `status` remains at its initialized value `0`, causing the code to misinterpret an empty response as status `0`. Check that `ret` is at least `sizeof(status)` bytes:\n\n```cpp\n\tuint8_t status \u003d 0;\n\tint ret \u003d libusb_control_transfer(dev_handle_, kBmReqD2hStdDev,\n\t\t\t\t\t  kRtsStdGetStatus, 0, 0, \u0026status,\n\t\t\t\t\t  sizeof(status), kUsbCtrlTimeoutMs);\n\n\tif (ret \u003c static_cast\u003cint\u003e(sizeof(status))) {\n\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"Error: GET_STATUS failed: %s\\n\",\n\t\t\tret \u003c 0 ? libusb_error_name(ret) : \"short read\");\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/46b34316-d342-48c7-a7f3-1c5d7cf82dbc)",
